Patch from MiniMyth2 project

Developed-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>



From c78c9e1060f408658abbb3497c41b9ca832f64e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:40:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] media: amlogic: amvdec: don't disable the HEVC front-end
 clock twice

When enabling "vdec_hevc" fails, __vdec_hevc_start() disabled
"vdec_hevcf" and returned the error, and its only caller,
amvdec_hevc_start(), then disabled "vdec_hevcf" again on that error.
Leave it to the caller, which enabled it.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/amvdec_hevc.c | 5 +----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/amvdec_hevc.c b/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/amvdec_hevc.c
index bc5c68b..94b393b 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/amvdec_hevc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/amvdec_hevc.c
@@ -427,11 +427,8 @@ static int __vdec_hevc_start(struct amvdec_session *sess)
 
 	clk_set_rate(core->amvdec_hevc_clk, 666666666);
 	ret = clk_prepare_enable(core->amvdec_hevc_clk);
-	if (ret) {
-		if (amvdec_hevc_has_hevcf(core))
-			clk_disable_unprepare(core->amvdec_hevcf_clk);
+	if (ret)
 		return ret;
-	}
 
 	if (core->pd_list) {
 		ret = meson_amvdec_power_domain_on(core, AMVDEC_PD_HEVC);
-- 
